.TH TENSOR-GPU-LEASE 1 "2026-11-24" "Tensor" "GPU Admission"
.SH NAME
tensor-gpu-lease \- simulated GPU lease lifecycle (Stage 2)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B python3 shared/scripts/tensor-gpu-lease.py --help
.SH DESCRIPTION
Stage 2 provides a Python-only, fail-closed GPU reservation state machine with
an injected backend interface and synthetic unit tests. It has no real systemd,
wallpaper, NVIDIA, Ollama, Hermes or MinerU backend and cannot change live GPU
or desktop state.  Production integration is prohibited until the relevant
adapters and idle signals have passed independent acceptance testing.
.PP
The manager keeps state in a caller-owned 0700 directory and a 0600 SQLite
file. The future adapter must verify GPU memory release before restoring
previously running wallpaper services; an unexpected wallpaper restart during
an active lease must be contained. Explicit foreground requests bypass idle
eligibility only, never conflicting resource ownership.
.SH SAFETY
Do not use the synthetic fake backend as an actual GPU-free-memory test. Do not
treat model server uptime, process existence, or arbitrary free-VRAM thresholds
as proof that no inference is active. All runtime clients must participate
before global scheduling guarantees can be claimed.
.SH SOURCE
iragonforce/ops shared/scripts/tensor-gpu-lease.py
